main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ braced sibling arg does not match base-inherited ctor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
does not uniquely resolve
--
N5008 [over.match.ctor]/1, [namespace.udecl]/3: base-class constructors are not
candidates for initializing a derived object unless inherited via a
using-declaration.  A brace-init-list of a sibling type (sharing a common base)
must not be viable for a class through the base's inherited copy constructor.
Regression test for the "symbol 'codet' does not uniquely resolve" front-end
bug (std_code.h): exprt and source_locationt both derive from irept, and
codet(dstringt, source_locationt) was spuriously viable for
codet(ID_assume, {std::move(expr)}).
